1
00:00:00,383 --> 00:00:04,076
In October 2026, Ledger confirmed
that hardware wallets sold

2
00:00:04,126 --> 00:00:07,595
through a reseller in Southeast
Asia had an extra circuit board

3
00:00:07,645 --> 00:00:11,735
hidden inside. It reads the recovery
phrase during setup and sends it out

4
00:00:11,785 --> 00:00:15,393
over a cellular link. Ledger's
Genuine Check still passes,

5
00:00:15,443 --> 00:00:19,666
because the secure chip itself is
untouched. This is tamper-check:

6
00:00:19,716 --> 00:00:22,633
software that looks for the
physical change instead.

7
00:00:23,647 --> 00:00:25,459
The primary signal is weight.

8
00:00:25,509 --> 00:00:29,774
On a milligram scale, take at least three
readings and re-zero between each one.

9
00:00:29,824 --> 00:00:31,581
They're averaged and compared with a

10
00:00:31,631 --> 00:00:33,776
reference unit from the
same production batch.

11
00:00:33,826 --> 00:00:37,897
The reference weights in this demo are
example values, not official specs.

12
00:00:37,947 --> 00:00:41,972
This unit is within tolerance,
its center of mass hasn't moved,

13
00:00:42,022 --> 00:00:46,826
and it is silent on RF, so the
verdict is likely genuine, risk zero.

14
00:00:47,811 --> 00:00:49,872
Now a blob of glue on one side.

15
00:00:49,922 --> 00:00:54,144
It adds a few hundred milligrams,
which a precision scale easily catches.

16
00:00:54,194 --> 00:00:58,093
In the 3D view, green marks
the expected center of mass,

17
00:00:58,143 --> 00:01:01,411
yellow the estimated one, and
red the region where mass seems

18
00:01:01,461 --> 00:01:04,856
to have been added. Center
of mass is an optional check,

19
00:01:04,906 --> 00:01:07,436
measured by tilting the device
over a pivot with a phone.

20
00:01:07,486 --> 00:01:11,752
The verdict is suspicious, and
a remediation checklist appears.

21
00:01:12,731 --> 00:01:14,697
Next, a simulated implant.

22
00:01:14,747 --> 00:01:18,963
The device is powered off inside a
Faraday bag while a radio scanner listens.

23
00:01:19,013 --> 00:01:22,653
A Ledger has no cellular radio,
so any burst in the cellular

24
00:01:22,703 --> 00:01:26,067
bands is critical. Here they
repeat about every thirty seconds,

25
00:01:26,117 --> 00:01:29,292
shown as red rings. But
silence isn't proof:

26
00:01:29,342 --> 00:01:33,349
an implant may only transmit
after setup. Weight plus RF:

27
00:01:33,399 --> 00:01:36,731
tampered, do not use, risk one hundred.

28
00:01:37,723 --> 00:01:39,083
What about a kitchen scale?

29
00:01:39,133 --> 00:01:42,405
With one-gram resolution, the
same measurement looks fine,

30
00:01:42,455 --> 00:01:44,750
and the tool warns that this is demo-only.

31
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:47,104
It cannot catch milligram-level implants.

32
00:01:48,111 --> 00:01:50,903
With a milligram scale, the
extra three hundred milligrams

33
00:01:50,953 --> 00:01:52,071
are flagged right away.

34
00:01:52,121 --> 00:01:55,252
The verdict and risk score come
from simple rules you can read.

35
00:01:55,302 --> 00:01:56,822
Then follow the checklist:

36
00:01:56,872 --> 00:01:58,964
do not enter a seed on this device.

37
00:01:59,014 --> 00:02:01,567
Run Genuine Check and
confirm the firmware,

38
00:02:01,617 --> 00:02:03,721
but remember it can't see added boards.

39
00:02:03,771 --> 00:02:06,496
If funds were ever on a
seed from this device,

40
00:02:06,546 --> 00:02:10,367
move them to a new wallet bought
directly from Ledger, with a new seed.

41
00:02:10,417 --> 00:02:15,518
Report it, and only then open the device
to inspect. Weigh before you trust.
